/*
box3dxt.lcb - xTalk Builder (LCB) binding library for Box3D, via the
              box3d_shim C shim. Part of box3dxt for OpenXTalk (OXT).

Once this extension is loaded, every public handler below is callable
directly from xTalk script, e.g.
    put b3WorldCreate(0, -10, 0, 1) into sWorld

Conventions (the shim, src/box3d_shim.c, is where each is enforced):
  * Handles are integers (0 = invalid). Every handler tolerates a stale or 0
    handle: getters return 0 or empty, actions do nothing.
  * NAMES ARE MECHANICAL: the handler for the shim's b3x_body_set_position is
    b3BodySetPosition; nothing is renamed by hand. tools/check-lcb-signatures.py
    holds the bijection (every export bound once, every binding wrapped by the
    one public handler of that name).
  * Distances are METRES, angles RADIANS, y is up. A rotation is a quaternion,
    x y z w.
  * A result of several numbers comes back as TEXT, comma-separated, with a
    "." decimal point in every locale: "x,y,z". The boundary carries one value
    per call, and one call returning three numbers is cheaper than three calls.
    Text crosses as a Pointer that textOf() copies, never as ZStringNative.
  * A yes/no crosses the public boundary as a Boolean and the C boundary as
    an int (asInt() below; `tR is not 0` on the way back).
  * Nothing here throws, bar the ABI check: a refused call returns 0 or empty
    and b3LastError() says why. A physics call in a frame loop must not be
    able to stop the loop.

The foreign handlers bind to the shared library "box3dxt" (built by
CMakeLists.txt). Bindings resolve on first use, so the library only needs to
be present at run time.

The module is org.openxtalk.library.boxthreed, not ...box3dxt: lc-compile
warns on a digit in a namespace component ("may cause future syntax error")
and the Extension Builder runs it with -Werror, which is what made box2dxt
need a builder of its own. A digit-free name costs nothing.
*/

/**
Bindings to Box3D, a 3D rigid-body physics engine by Erin Catto.

A world holds bodies; a body carries shapes (its collision geometry and
material) and can be linked to other bodies by joints. Worlds, bodies,
shapes and joints are integer handles. 0 means a call was refused or found
nothing, and a stale handle is harmless: getters return 0 or empty, actions
do nothing. <b3LastError> says why a call was refused.

Every distance is in metres and every angle in radians, with y pointing up.
Keep moving objects roughly 0.1 to 10 metres across. Create a world with
<b3WorldCreate>, give it bodies with <b3BodyCreate> and shapes with the
b3ShapeAdd calls, advance it with <b3WorldStep> at a fixed time step, then
read every body that moved with <b3WorldUpdateMoves>.

A rotation is a quaternion, four numbers x, y, z, w; <b3QuatFromAxisAngle>
and <b3QuatFromEuler> make one. A result of several numbers (a position, a
rotation, a bounding box) comes back as comma-separated text such as
"1.5,0,-2", so item 1 of it is x. Lists (the shapes of a body, ray hits,
events) are taken as a snapshot by one call and read back with small
getters; their indices are 1-based.

Box3D decides nothing about drawing: this library computes where things
are, and the stack draws them however it likes.

Tags: Physics, 3D, Library
*/
library org.openxtalk.library.boxthreed

use com.livecode.foreign

-- The engine's own string builder, resolved by NAME (so no leading
-- underscore): see textOf() below.
foreign handler MCStringCreateWithBytes(in pBytes as Pointer, in pByteCount as CUInt, in pEncoding as CUInt, in pIsExternalRep as CBool, out rString as String) returns CBool binds to "<builtin>"

metadata title is "Box3D for OpenXTalk"
metadata author is "Seth Morrow Software"
metadata version is "0.1.0"
metadata summary is "3D rigid-body physics for xTalk via Box3D (bodies, shapes, joints, ray casts, events)."

-- =====================================================================
-- Foreign bindings to the shim (private). One per export of
-- src/box3d_shim.c; tools/check-lcb-signatures.py holds every line to the
-- C definition it binds (name, return type, each parameter type).
-- =====================================================================

-- ---- the library
private foreign handler _abi_version() returns CInt binds to "c:box3dxt>b3x_abi_version!cdecl"
