/**
Summary: Pushes every body near a point away from it.

pWorld: A world handle from <b3WorldCreate>.

pX: The x of the centre of the blast.

pY: The y of the centre.

pZ: The z of the centre.

pRadius: The radius of full strength, in metres.

pFalloff: How far beyond the radius the push fades to nothing.

pImpulse: The push per square metre of surface facing the blast. Negative
pulls.
*/
public handler b3WorldExplode(in pWorld as Integer, in pX as Number, in pY as Number, in pZ as Number, in pRadius as Number, in pFalloff as Number, in pImpulse as Number) returns nothing
   unsafe
      _world_explode(pWorld, pX, pY, pZ, pRadius, pFalloff, pImpulse)
   end unsafe
end handler

-- =====================================================================
-- Bodies
-- =====================================================================

/**
Summary: Creates a body in a world.

pWorld: A world handle from <b3WorldCreate>.

pType: The body type: 0 static, 1 kinematic, 2 dynamic.

pX: The x of its position, in metres.

pY: The y of its position.

pZ: The z of its position.

Returns: A body handle, or 0 if the arguments were refused.

Example:
put b3BodyCreate(sWorld, 2, 0, 5, 0) into tBall
get b3ShapeAddSphere(tBall, 0, 0, 0, 0.5, 1, 0.6, 0.2)

Description: A static body never moves (floors, walls); a kinematic body
moves only as it is told; a dynamic body is moved by forces and collisions.
A body has no size until it is given shapes with the b3ShapeAdd calls, and a
dynamic body has no mass until then: give a body its shapes before joining
it to another.
*/
public handler b3BodyCreate(in pWorld as Integer, in pType as Integer, in pX as Number, in pY as Number, in pZ as Number) returns Integer
   variable tR as Integer
   unsafe
      put _body_create(pWorld, pType, pX, pY, pZ) into tR
   end unsafe
   return tR
end handler

/**
Summary: Creates a body in a world, already turned.

pWorld: A world handle from <b3WorldCreate>.

pType: The body type: 0 static, 1 kinematic, 2 dynamic.

pX: The x of its position, in metres.

pY: The y of its position.

pZ: The z of its position.

pQx: The x part of the rotation quaternion.

pQy: The y part of the rotation quaternion.

pQz: The z part of the rotation quaternion.

pQw: The w (scalar) part of the rotation quaternion.

Returns: A body handle, or 0 if the arguments were refused.

Description: As <b3BodyCreate>, with a starting rotation.
<b3QuatFromAxisAngle> and <b3QuatFromEuler> make the quaternion.
*/
public handler b3BodyCreateRotated(in pWorld as Integer, in pType as Integer, in pX as Number, in pY as Number, in pZ as Number, in pQx as Number, in pQy as Number, in pQz as Number, in pQw as Number) returns Integer
   variable tR as Integer
   unsafe
      put _body_create_rotated(pWorld, pType, pX, pY, pZ, pQx, pQy, pQz, pQw) into tR
   end unsafe
   return tR
end handler

/**
Summary: Destroys a body, its shapes and the joints attached to it.

pBody: A body handle from <b3BodyCreate>.
*/
public handler b3BodyDestroy(in pBody as Integer) returns nothing
   unsafe
