Summary: Returns the position and rotation of a body as a matrix.

pBody: A body handle from <b3BodyCreate>.

Returns: Twelve numbers as text: the three columns of the rotation matrix (x
axis, y axis, z axis), then the position.

Description: For renderers that take a matrix: the first nine numbers are
where the body's own x, y and z axes point in the world.
*/
public handler b3BodyMatrix(in pBody as Integer) returns String
   variable tP as Pointer
   unsafe
      put _body_matrix(pBody) into tP
   end unsafe
   return textOf(tP)
end handler

/**
Summary: Moves a body to a position and rotation at once.

pBody: A body handle from <b3BodyCreate>.

pX: The x coordinate.

pY: The y coordinate.

pZ: The z coordinate.

pQx: The x part of the rotation quaternion.

pQy: The y part of the rotation quaternion.

pQz: The z part of the rotation quaternion.

pQw: The w (scalar) part of the rotation quaternion.

Description: A teleport: it does not sweep, so it can put a body inside
another. To move a kinematic body smoothly, use <b3BodySetTargetTransform>
or a velocity.
*/
public handler b3BodySetTransform(in pBody as Integer, in pX as Number, in pY as Number, in pZ as Number, in pQx as Number, in pQy as Number, in pQz as Number, in pQw as Number) returns nothing
   unsafe
      _body_set_transform(pBody, pX, pY, pZ, pQx, pQy, pQz, pQw)
   end unsafe
end handler

